-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",38,{
[1185]="7006AD88\n1\tDefeat smugglers in Tâkhdar (total: 6)\tSmugglers can be found throughout Tâkhdar. Ilzhâna has asked you to thin the number of smugglers stalking Tâkhdar and interfering in her trade. She insists it's for the safety of the cellars, not because they are business rivals.\n2\tSpeak to Ilzhâna\tIlzhâna can be found at Tilmakhím on the western side of Tâkhdar. Return to Ilzhâna with news of your exploits.\n",
[1186]="70027209\n1\tTalk to Rhuwalhan at his home in Barnavon\tRhuwalhan Brehur is at his home in Upper Barnavon. Eres has asked you to speak with Rhuwalhan Brehur and convince him to release the hostages he took to force the men of the Boar-clan to work the mine.\n2\tTalk to Eres in Barnavon\tEres is in Lower Barnavon. You should return to Eres with news of Rhuwalhan's refusal and defeat.\n",
[1187]="70007048\n1\tDeliver the necklace to its rightful owner\tYou discovered a necklace upon one of the half-orcs in the central Lone-lands. Perhaps you can ask some of the Eglain if they know who the true owner of the necklace could be.\n",
[1188]="7004D70D\n1\tPiles of stone blocks can be found in Erebor, logs can be found in the halls of Felegoth, crates of rations can be found throughout Dale, and barrels of water can be found in Lake-town. King Thorin III has asked you to aid the peoples of the North in preparing for battle against Vethúg Wintermind.\t\n2\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III can be found in the Hall Under the Mountain. You have mistaken King Thorin's jest for an actual task. You should return to King Thorin.\n3\tTalk to Erna\030Talk to Dagrun\030Talk to Thranduil\tErna can be found in Dale, Dagrun can be found in Lake-town, and Thranduil can be found in Felegoth. King Thorin III has asked you to deliver a message of warning to the other strongholds of the North and ask that they prepare their defences as best they can before Vethúg Wintermind strikes.\n4\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III can be found in the Hall Under the Mountain. You have warned the leaders of the strongholds of the North to prepare for the coming of Vethúg Wintermind as King Thorin asked. You should return to King Thorin.\n",
[1189]="70062DE4\n1\tLook out over the flooded city from the northern piece of the Great Bridge\030Find the northern part of the Great Bridge for Caron\030Defeat Orcs in Tharbad (total: 8)\tCaron has asked you to defeat Orcs, who have no place in Tharbad as once it was. She also wants you to look from the northern piece of the Great Bridge that still stands above the water, and tell her what you see.\n2\tTalk to Caron on the river-bank west of Tharbad\tCaron is west of Tharbad, on the banks of the river.\n",
[1190]="7005F866\n1\tTalk to Thrástan\tThrástan can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn. After you and Hersegg discovered an old dwarf alone in the caverns of Gloomingtarn, Hermáth Stormhammer has asked you to talk to Thrástan and uncover how he came to dwell in Mount Gundabad. You should talk to Thrástan.\n2\tHail Thrástan and try to get his attention\tThrástan can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn. Thrástan seems unaware of your presence. You should hail Thrástan and attempt to get his attention.\n3\tTalk to Thrástan\tThrástan can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn. Thrástan has turned to look at you. You should talk to Thrástan.\n4\tCalm Thrástan and urge him to continue\tThrástan can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn. Thrástan has become distraught in his attempt to answer your questions. You should try to calm Thrástan and urge him to continue trying to remember.\n5\tTalk to Thrástan\tThrástan can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn. Thrástan does not appear to be able to answer your questions. You should talk to Thrástan.\n6\tTalk to Hermáth Stormhammer\tHermáth Stormhammer can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn. Before you could learn much from Thrástan, the old dwarf appears to suffer from some unseen ailment. You should talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.\n",
[1191]="7004CE92\n1\tTalk to the messenger\tThe messenger stands before King Bard II, inside the Great-keep in Dale. You should hear the messenger's tidings.\n2\tTalk to Prince Bryn\tKing Bard II, Queen Regent Erna, and Prince Bryn stand discussing the messenger's tidings in the Great-keep in Dale. You should hear what Prince Bryn has to say in response to the messenger.\n3\tTalk to Queen Regent Erna\030Talk to King Bard II\tKing Bard II, Queen Regent Erna, and Prince Bryn stand discussing the messenger's tidings in the Great-keep in Dale. You should hear what King Bard II and his regent mother, Erna, have to say in response to Prince Bryn and the messenger.\n4\tGo with the messenger\tYou should talk to the messenger who stands before King Bard II in the Great-keep in Dale, and learn where you must go to investigate the report of violence.\n5\tTalk to Enkárvo\tYou should speak to Enkárvo, the man of Dorwinion, in the refugee camp, across the river from Dale.\n",
[1192]="7000A139\n1\tDefeat sand-nerbyg in the Barandalf (total: 12)\030Defeat huge sand-nerbyg in the Barandalf (total: 2)\tSand-nerbyg can be found in great numbers on the Barandalf, on either side of the road that runs through the sand dunes along the west side of the Brandywine. Mundaric Sandheaver has asked you to defeat sand-nerbyg on the Barandalf before they swarm, bringing destruction in whichever direction their paths take them.\n2\tTalk to Mundaric Sandheaver in Dwaling\tMundaric Sandheaver is at Dwaling, south of the Barandalf. You have defeated many of the sand-nerbyg that have been breeding on the Barandalf and should return to Mundaric Sandheaver with news of your victories.\n",
[1193]="7006906B\n1\tInvestigate the source of the disturbance below deck\tInvestigate the source of the disturbance below deck.\n2\tDefeat crab hunters (total: 10)\030Defeat great crabs (total: 8)\030Seal hull leaks (total: 8)\tProtect the Khâlbina and her crew from crabs that have boarded the ship!\n3\tDefeat greater crabs (total: 2)\tDefeat the greater crabs!\n",
[1194]="70020EEC\n1\tTalk to Laurel Sackville in Frerin's Court\tThe Inn League Tasting is taking place in Frerin's Court, in the southern outdoor courtyard of Thorin's Hall. You may only speak with the recruiter when she is not distracted by her duties. You should go to the Inn League Tasting and see what you can do to sabotage it. Jónar has expressed that he does not want any more dwarves joining the Inn League while he still draws breath!\n2\tHide behind the nearby kegs until Laurel Sackville wanders away\tThe tasting table is in Frerin's Court, just to the south of Thorin's Hall. You should wait for Laurel Sackville, the Inn League Recruiter, to wander away.\n3\tAdd swill to Inn League samples (total: 8)\tThe tasting table is in Frerin's Court, just to the south of Thorin's Hall. You should add swill to the tasting samples between rounds of tasting. Surely no one will notice.... This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tWatch the events of the tasting unfold\tThe tasting has begun! You must watch the carnage unfold, for Jónar will wish to hear of your success. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\tTalk to Jónar in Thorin's Hall\tJónar awaits word of your deeds in the inn at Thorin's Hall. You should tell Jónar of your cruel, wonderful success against the Inn League Tasting recruiter.\n",
[1195]="700000B6\n1\tTalk to Hazel Kenton\tHazel Kenton, a captain of great renown, is at the West-gate of Bree-town, in the Bree-land. You have been told to speak with Captain Kenton if you wish to better yourself.\n2\tCollect Harper's badge\tAldis Oatbearer has been seen at Brigand's Watch, north of the Old Sweetgrass farm west of Bree. Hilton Harper is at Thornley's work-site, north-west of the town. Captain Kenton has asked you to recover Hilton Harper's badge from Aldis Oatbearer, the brigand that stole it.\n3\tBring Harper's badge to Hilton Harper\tHilton Harper is at Thornley's work-site, north-west of Bree-town. Now that you have recovered the stolen badge, returning it to Hilton Harper might restore his confidence and inspire him to rejoin the fight against the brigands menacing the Bree-fields.\n4\tTalk to Hazel Kenton\tCaptain Kenton is at the West-gate of Bree-town. Hazel Kenton will want to know that you have successfully restored Hilton Harper's will to defend the Bree-fields from those who threaten the peace.\n",
[1196]="7002C5F2\n1\tDefeat Easterlings throughout the Brown Lands (total: 8)\030Defeat Khundolar Message-shouter (total: 2)\tEasterlings can be found throughout the Brown Lands, and message-shouters can be found near their established foothold at Lashkarg. Gamal has asked you to defeat Easterlings throughout the Brown Lands, and also to defeat some of the message-shouters that use the name Khoratón.\n2\tTalk to Gamal\tGamal is in the Brown Lands, south of Etheburg. You have defeated some of the Khundolar Easterlings in the Brown Lands and should return now to Gamal.\n",
[1197]="7005A664\n1\tAssist Varthmath with \"Exploring Vâr Nuchur\"\030Assist Varthmath with \"Exploring Brúvraum\"\tVarthmath can be found at Maergrind, The Noble Gate of Máttugard. You should assist Varthmath with his expedition in Máttugard.\n2\tTravel to Asbaj-khîrfin\tAsbaj-khîrfin can be found in the northern reaches of Máttugard. You should travel to Asbaj-khîrfin.\n3\tTalk to Varthmath at Asbaj-khîrfin\tAsbaj-khîrfin can be found in the northern reaches of Máttugard. You should talk to Varthmath at Asbaj-khîrfin.\n4\tTest the grodbog hive samples (total: 2)\tA workbench can be found at Asbaj-khîrfin. At the workbench, you should test the samples you have acquired.\n5\tTalk to Varthmath at Asbaj-khîrfin\tAsbaj-khîrfin can be found in the northern reaches of Máttugard. You should talk to Varthmath at Asbaj-khîrfin.\n",
[1198]="70027AC8\n1\tCollect plans for the invasion of Trum Dreng\tThe chieftain of the Dragon-clan invaders can surely be found at the main house in the Herd-lands, looking down upon the farm from on high. You should kill the chieftain and steal the plans for the invasion of Trum Dreng by the Dragon-clan.\n2\tBring the map of the invasion route to Blodwen\tBlodwen awaits you in her hiding place near the river in the Herd-lands. You should return to Blodwen with the map you found and with the dire news that Murig has escaped you.\n",
[1199]="7002CAEA\n1\tInvestigate Stanric's house\tStanric's house is near the Mead Hall in Stangard. You should investigate Stanric's house, and do your best to keep beneath the notice of the residents of Stangard using what sneaking skill you can muster.\n2\tInvestigate the glinting item\tSomething glints on the floor of Stanric's house in Stangard. You should investigate the glinting object more closely.\n3\tAsk Cynred why his jail-keys were on the floor of Stanric's home\tCynred is at the lock-house in Stangard. You should find Cynred and ask him why his jail keys are in Stanric's home.\n4\tFind Stanric in the lock-house\tAccording to Cynred, Stanric is down below in the lock-house. You should find Stanric at once.\n",
[1200]="7002B7FB\n1\tSpeak with the Festival Announcer, Caltha Tunnelly, at the Farmers Faire in Bywater\tCaltha Tunnelly, the Festival Announcer, can be found in Bywater while the Farmers Faire is in town. You should speak with Caltha Tunnelly to learn about the Farmers Faire.\n",
[1201]="7002513D\n1\tTalk to the new Festival Stable-master in West Bree\030Talk to the new Festival Stable-master in Celondim\030Talk to the new Festival Stable-master in Thorin's Hall\030Talk to the new Festival Stable-master in Michel Delving\tMany events are featured in the Yule Festival this year. Notable places to visit include: -The Thorin's Hall Inn -The Horsefields Festival Grounds (Bree) -The Party Tree (the Shire) -The Duillond Festival Area -The new Winter Region of Frostbluff This notice is meant to direct you to the new festival area.\n",
[1202]="7001BB56\n1\tTalk to Opal Goodbody at the Party Tree\tOpal Goodbody can be found at the Party Tree in Hobbiton, a fair Shire-town. You should speak with Opal Goodbody, who will illuminate this year's festival events for you.\n",
[1203]="70020D7F\n1\tTalk to Maengamiel in Duillond's garden\030Speak with Gil Plover at the Hedge Maze in Bree's Horsefields\tThe Hedge Maze can be found in the Horsefields of Bree, and the Stomp-a-Shrew event can be found in Duillond. You should visit the two respective events if you wish to learn more of them.\n",
[1204]="7001EB9D\n1\tTalk to Gísli Strongclub in Thorin's Hall\tGísli Strongclub can be found inside the new Festival Arena, an ale-hall inside of Thorin's Hall. You should speak with Gísli Strongclub, who will illuminate this year's festival events for you.\n",
[1205]="7000AC53\n1\tDeliver the ore to Soldier Glat at Tol Ascarnen\030Collect Unrefined Isendeep Ore (total: 5)\tIron ore can be found on the dwarves who fight for the Free Peoples or from the Isendeep Mine to the north. Angmar's army is shoring up the defences at Tol Ascarnen. Glat intends to build a massive iron pot to heat oil with which to douse the Free Peoples who attempt to assail the keep.\n",
[1206]="70020AA6\n1\tConvince Óli of Thorin's Hall to abandon the Inn League\tÓli can be found in Thorin's Hall, in the very inn where Jónar himself stands. Jónar has demanded that you approach dwarves from Thorin's Hall that have joined the Inn League and harass them until they abandon this folly to take up arms with the Ale Association instead.\n2\tÓli is still unconvinced; you should try again.\tÓli can be found in Thorin's Hall, in the very inn where Jónar himself stands. Jónar has demanded that you approach dwarves from Thorin's Hall that have joined the Inn League and harass them until they abandon this folly to take up arms with the Ale Association instead.\n3\tÓli still looks unconvinced; you should try again.\tÓli can be found in Thorin's Hall, in the very inn where Jónar himself stands. Jónar has demanded that you approach dwarves from Thorin's Hall that have joined the Inn League and harass them until they abandon this folly to take up arms with the Ale Association instead.\n4\tConvince Kópur of Noglond to abandon the Inn League\tKópur, a member of the Inn League, can be found in Noglond in Ered Luin, south of Thorin's Hall in the Vale of Thrain. Jónar has demanded that you approach dwarves from Thorin's Hall that have joined the Inn League and harass them until they abandon this folly to take up arms with the Ale Association instead.\n5\tKópur is not convinced -- you should try again\tKópur, a member of the Inn League, can be found in Noglond in Ered Luin, south of Thorin's Hall in the Vale of Thrain. Jónar has demanded that you approach dwarves from Thorin's Hall that have joined the Inn League and harass them until they abandon this folly to take up arms with the Ale Association instead.\n6\tKópur is still not convinced -- one more time\tKópur, a member of the Inn League, can be found in Noglond in Ered Luin, south of Thorin's Hall in the Vale of Thrain. Jónar has demanded that you approach dwarves from Thorin's Hall that have joined the Inn League and harass them until they abandon this folly to take up arms with the Ale Association instead.\n7\tConvince Grímar of Gondamon to abandon the Inn League\tGrímar, a member of the Inn League, can be found in Gondamon in the very centre of Ered Luin. Jónar has demanded that you approach dwarves from Thorin's Hall that have joined the Inn League and harass them until they abandon this folly to take up arms with the Ale Association instead.\n8\tGrímar does not seem convinced; try again\tGrímar, a member of the Inn League, can be found in Gondamon in the very centre of Ered Luin. Jónar has demanded that you approach dwarves from Thorin's Hall that have joined the Inn League and harass them until they abandon this folly to take up arms with the Ale Association instead.\n9\tGrímar is still not convinced -- try once more\tGrímar, a member of the Inn League, can be found in Gondamon in the very centre of Ered Luin. Jónar has demanded that you approach dwarves from Thorin's Hall that have joined the Inn League and harass them until they abandon this folly to take up arms with the Ale Association instead.\n10\tConvince Herluf of Needlehole to abandon the Inn League\tHerluf can be found in Needlehole, a hobbit town with many dwarf inhabitants in the north-west corner of the Shire. Jónar has demanded that you approach dwarves from Thorin's Hall that have joined the Inn League and harass them until they abandon this folly to take up arms with the Ale Association instead.\n11\tHerluf is still not convinced; you should try again\tHerluf can be found in Needlehole, a hobbit town with many dwarf inhabitants in the north-west corner of the Shire. Jónar has demanded that you approach dwarves from Thorin's Hall that have joined the Inn League and harass them until they abandon this folly to take up arms with the Ale Association instead.\n12\tHerluf is a stubborn fool! Try again\tHerluf can be found in Needlehole, a hobbit town with many dwarf inhabitants in the north-west corner of the Shire. Jónar has demanded that you approach dwarves from Thorin's Hall that have joined the Inn League and harass them until they abandon this folly to take up arms with the Ale Association instead.\n13\tTalk to Jónar in Thorin's Hall\tJónar awaits you in Thorin's Hall. You should return to Jónar with the encouraging news that you were able to bully the Inn League dwarves into abandoning their foolish pursuits.\n",
[1207]="7000A174\n1\tTalk to Calenglad\tCalenglad is at the Ranger camp on the island of Tinnudir, west of the road that runs through Parth Aduial and the cross-roads of Canadiach. Torogethir has asked you to bring word to Calenglad that his efforts on the Fields of Fornost are going well, and that Calenglad should focus on combatting the tomb-robbers that plague Evendim.\n",
[1208]="70043DA7\n1\tDefeat crebain (total: 15)\tCrebain can be found on the Western side of Osgiliath. You should defeat crebain.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many spying crebain.\n",
[1209]="70025CC2\n1\tTalk to Orchalwë at Tinnudir\tOrchalwë is at Tinnudir, south of Rantost. Orchalwë wants to speak with you about what is next for Evendim.\n",
[1210]="7006C57A\n1\tDeliver oasis water to the shade of the ruined khanâg\tAítarshun asked you to help him fulfil an oath forsaken to a man who perished in the ruined khanâg north of Shonith. He gave you a phial of oasis water and bid you deliver it to the shade.\n2\tInform Aítarsun at Shonith his oath is fulfilled\tThe shade faded from existence. The man is at peace, though it was displeased with Aítarshun. Return to the Elf at Shonith and tell him what occurred.\n",
[1211]="7002F893\n1\tDefeat Orc-ambushers south of the road to Elthengels (total: 8)\tOrc-ambushers have been frequently seen south of the road leading west from Elthengels. Guthléod has asked you to assault the ambushers directly in the hopes of preventing more of their attacks on unwary travellers.\n2\tReturn to Guthléod at the merchants' camp\tGuthléod can be found at his tent at the trader's outpost, west of the village of Elthengels. You have defeated many of the Orc-ambushers and should inform Guthléod that his request has been fulfilled.\n",
[1212]="7006C530\n1\tCollect drams of sand-sifter blood ([see journal]/10)\tZidemel the zealot told Andur his bloodline would live on if he provided the desert a hefty gift of blood. Andur asked that you collect the blood of sand-sifters so that he can fulfil this gift.\n2\tReturn the drams of sand-worm blood to Andur in Jirush\tYou ventured into the desert and collected ten drams of sand-sifter blood for Andur. Return the blood to Andur at Jirush. He is listening to Zidemel preach in the centre of the outpost.\n",
[1213]="70000C36\n1\tDeliver the fur and haunches to Frideric\030Collect Warg-furs (total: 6)\030Collect boar-haunches (total: 6)\tBoars wander to the east between Ost Guruth and the Last Bridge, and Wargs wander the area near Ost Guruth along Great East Road. Frideric resides at the Eglain Ruin-hold of Ost Guruth, north of the Great East Road in the Lone-lands. Frideric asked you to help him gather a peace offering of boar-haunches and Warg-fur for the strange creatures living near the Last Bridge at the eastern end of the Great East Road.\n",
[1214]="70000C37\n1\tDeliver the salted-meats and furs to the creatures' leader\tThe creatures' encampment is south of the Great East Road near the Tornstones, south and a little east of Ost Guruth. Frideric the Elder provided you with a crate of salted meats and furs to deliver as a peace offering to the creatures near the Tornstones.\n",
[1215]="7006B673\n1\tCollect pork loins from fen-wallowers (total: 4)\030Collect beans (total: 4)\030Collect fresh herbs (total: 3)\tEndunâm has asked you to collect beans found along the road travelling north-east to the old salt mines. He also needs pork loins from wild boars and fresh herbs, both from Shegdush far to the east.\n2\tBring the ingredients to Endunâm in Iridír\tYou have collected the meat, beans, and herbs for which Endunâm asked. You should bring the ingredients to him in Iridír.\n",
[1216]="7004CF34\n1\tTalk to Thranduil\tThranduil can be found in Felegoth. You should talk to Thranduil about the attack on the Elves at the caravan.\n2\tCollect sap from trees (total: 6)\tYou should collect sap from trees in Eryn Lasgalen that the Elves have already tapped for sap collection.\n3\tLay a trap to catch one of Iphantemel's spawn\tThe last place anyone saw spiders was near the caravan that was attacked. You should use the sap to lay a trap for the spiders.\n4\tWait and watch the trap\tThe last place anyone saw spiders was near the caravan that was attacked. You should wait and watch the trap to see if any spiders come.\n5\tTalk to Thranduil\tThranduil can be found in Felegoth. You should speak with Thranduil about the failed trap.\n6\tCollect corrupted sap from Huorns (total: 6)\tThe sap can be taken from corrupted Huorns throughout Eryn Lasgalen. You should collect corrupted sap for a second attempt at laying a trap.\n7\tSet up another trap to catch a spider\030Catch a spider\tA good place for a trap might be closer to Felegoth, near the main road that runs through Eryn Lasgalen. You should use the corrupted sap to lay a trap for the spiders.\n8\tBring the spider leg to Thranduil\tThranduil can be found in Felegoth. You should bring the spider leg to Thranduil.\n",
})
